    {
      "id": 141083,
      "name": "AlexxKay",
      "username": "AlexxKay",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/59ef9b/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2015-05-06T00:03:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>More generally, an effect that gives you a *specific* power use lets you use that power even if the \"one use of a power per turn\" would normally prevent it.</p><p>One significant example of this is with Expatriette.&nbsp; If she has Pride and Prejudice out, and is the recipient of a \"may use an additional power\" during her turn, she may (and probably should) do as follows:</p><p>* Use Prejudice (first power use).</p><p>* Use Pride (additional power use).</p><p>* Use Prejudice (because this is explicitly allowed by Pride, that overrides the normal once-per-turn rule).</p><p>When using Unload, save Pride until last, and you can get an extra use of Prejudice on top of all the power-uses that Unload allowed you.</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:18:06.574Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
