      "raw": "<p>More generally, an effect that gives you a *specific* power use lets you use that power even if the &quot;one use of a power per turn&quot; would normally prevent it.</p><p>One significant example of this is with Expatriette.&nbsp; If she has Pride and Prejudice out, and is the recipient of a &quot;may use an additional power&quot; during her turn, she may (and probably should) do as follows:</p><p>* Use Prejudice (first power use).</p><p>* Use Pride (additional power use).</p><p>* Use Prejudice (because this is explicitly allowed by Pride, that overrides the normal once-per-turn rule).</p><p>When using Unload, save Pride until last, and you can get an extra use of Prejudice on top of all the power-uses that Unload allowed you.</p>",
